    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0386" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg380"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill asks if this Government agrees to British proposal concerning
                    surplus indemnity, referred to in his telegram of the 10th instant.</p>
                <p>The Chinese plenipotentiaries are still waiting authorization of Chinese
                    Government to sign protocol.</p>
                <pb facs="0387" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/>
                <p>Mr. Rockhill will remain at Peking until the matter is settled.</p>
                <p>Replying to Mr. Hay’s telegram<anchor n="1" xml:id="d307-f1"/> to Mr. Conger,
                    composition of Commission for the revision of the tariff and place of meeting
                    not yet settled. * * *)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
